{"id":"ALG-P08","workedExamples":[{"id":"ALG-P08-we-01","title":"Multiplying (x + 3)(x + 5) with the area model — all four products","steps":[{"prompt":"Draw a 2-by-2 area box. The left side splits into x and 3; the top splits into x and 5. How many smaller rectangles (partial products) does that make?","reveal":"Four. Each piece of the left side pairs with each piece of the top, so 2 × 2 = 4 partial products. Missing any one of them changes the answer."},{"prompt":"Fill the two top boxes: x times the top pieces. What are x·x and x·5?","reveal":"x·x = x² and x·5 = 5x. The 5x is a real region of area — it is NOT optional."},{"prompt":"Fill the two bottom boxes: 3 times the top pieces. What are 3·x and 3·5?","reveal":"3·x = 3x and 3·5 = 15. The 3x is the other middle region."},{"prompt":"Add all four partial products: x² + 5x + 3x + 15. Combine like terms.","reveal":"The two middle terms 5x and 3x combine: 5x + 3x = 8x. So (x + 3)(x + 5) = x² + 8x + 15."},{"prompt":"Why is x² + 15 a wrong answer here?","reveal":"x² + 15 only multiplies the firsts (x·x) and the lasts (3·5) and throws away both middle regions. The area box proves 5x and 3x are real area — you must keep all FOUR products and combine the middle terms to 8x."}]},{"id":"ALG-P08-we-02","title":"Tracking signs in the middle: (x − 4)(x + 6)","steps":[{"prompt":"Rewrite (x − 4) as a sum so every sign is explicit. What is each term?","reveal":"x − 4 means x + (−4). The second term is negative four. Carrying that minus sign through every product is the whole game."},{"prompt":"Multiply the firsts and the lasts: x·x and (−4)·(+6).","reveal":"x·x = x² and (−4)·(+6) = −24. A negative times a positive is negative, so the last term is −24."},{"prompt":"Now the two middle products: x·(+6) and (−4)·x. What signs do they get?","reveal":"x·6 = +6x and (−4)·x = −4x. Keep the minus on the −4x; dropping it is the classic slip."},{"prompt":"Combine the middle terms: +6x and −4x.","reveal":"6x − 4x = 2x. The middle coefficient is +2, so (x − 4)(x + 6) = x² + 2x − 24."},{"prompt":"What goes wrong if you mishandle the sign and get −2x?","reveal":"Writing −4x + 6x correctly gives +2x. If you instead treat both middles as negative (or drop the +6), you get −2x and the wrong trinomial x² − 2x − 24. One sign slip flips the entire middle coefficient — always track each sign separately, then combine."}]}],"problems":{"p1":[{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"An outfield section is laid out (x + 3) feet by (x + 5) feet. Multiply (x + 3)(x + 5) to find its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 8x + 15","x^2 + 15","x^2 + 2x + 15","x^2 + 8x + 8"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 8x + 15"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 15":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 15":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Make four partial products: x·x, x·5, 3·x, 3·5.","Combine the middle terms 5x + 3x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A practice infield measures (x + 4) by (x + 6). Multiply (x + 4)(x + 6) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 24","x^2 + 24","x^2 + 10x + 10","x^2 + 2x + 24"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 24"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 24":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 24":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·6, 4·x, 4·6.","Add the middles: 6x + 4x = 10x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A bullpen mound area is (x − 4) by (x + 7). Multiply (x − 4)(x + 7).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 3x − 28","x^2 − 28","x^2 − 3x − 28","x^2 + 11x − 28"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 3x − 28"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 28":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 3x − 28":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Write x − 4 as x + (−4) and keep that sign.","Middle: +7x and −4x combine to +3x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A warning-track strip is (x − 5) by (x − 8). Multiply (x − 5)(x − 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 13x + 40","x^2 + 40","x^2 + 13x + 40","x^2 − 3x + 40"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 13x + 40"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 40":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 13x + 40":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middles are negative: −8x and −5x.","(−5)(−8) = +40, but −8x − 5x = −13x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-softball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A practice field is (x + 2) by (x + 4). Multiply (x + 2)(x + 4) to find its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 6x + 8","x^2 + 8","x^2 + 2x + 8","x^2 + 6x + 6"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 6x + 8"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 8":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 8":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·4, 2·x, 2·4.","Middle: 4x + 2x = 6x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-softball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A batting cage footprint is (x + 5) by (x + 7). Multiply (x + 5)(x + 7).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 12x + 35","x^2 + 35","x^2 + 12x + 12","x^2 + 2x + 35"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 12x + 35"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 35":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 35":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Build all four partial products first.","Combine 7x + 5x = 12x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-softball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A dugout extension is (x − 3) by (x + 9). Multiply (x − 3)(x + 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 6x − 27","x^2 − 27","x^2 − 6x − 27","x^2 + 12x − 27"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 6x − 27"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 27":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 6x − 27":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Keep the sign: x − 3 is x + (−3).","Middle: +9x and −3x give +6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-softball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A tarp section is (x − 6) by (x − 7). Multiply (x − 6)(x − 7).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 13x + 42","x^2 + 42","x^2 + 13x + 42","x^2 − x + 42"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 13x + 42"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 42":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 13x + 42":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middle terms are negative.","(−6)(−7) = +42, and −7x − 6x = −13x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-basketball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A practice court is (x + 4) by (x + 6). Multiply (x + 4)(x + 6) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 24","x^2 + 24","x^2 + 10x + 10","x^2 + 2x + 24"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 24"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 24":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 24":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·6, 4·x, 4·6.","Middle: 6x + 4x = 10x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-basketball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A court plus a safety border is (x + 3) by (x + 8). Multiply (x + 3)(x + 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 11x + 24","x^2 + 24","x^2 + 11x + 11","x^2 + 5x + 24"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 11x + 24"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 24":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 5x + 24":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Make all four partial products.","Combine 8x + 3x = 11x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-basketball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A resized key is (x − 2) by (x + 9). Multiply (x − 2)(x + 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 7x − 18","x^2 − 18","x^2 − 7x − 18","x^2 + 11x − 18"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 7x − 18"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 18":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 7x − 18":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["x − 2 is x + (−2); track that sign.","Middle: +9x and −2x give +7x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-basketball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A trimmed practice area is (x − 5) by (x − 9). Multiply (x − 5)(x − 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 14x + 45","x^2 + 45","x^2 + 14x + 45","x^2 − 4x + 45"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 14x + 45"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 45":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 14x + 45":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middle products are negative.","(−5)(−9) = +45, and −9x − 5x = −14x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-soccer-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A training grid is (x + 5) by (x + 8). Multiply (x + 5)(x + 8) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 13x + 40","x^2 + 40","x^2 + 13x + 13","x^2 + 3x + 40"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 13x + 40"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 40":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 3x + 40":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·8, 5·x, 5·8.","Middle: 8x + 5x = 13x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-soccer-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A resized pitch is (x + 6) by (x + 7). Multiply (x + 6)(x + 7).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 13x + 42","x^2 + 42","x^2 + 13x + 13","x^2 + x + 42"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 13x + 42"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 42":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + x + 42":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Build all four partial products first.","Combine 7x + 6x = 13x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-soccer-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A drill zone is (x − 3) by (x + 10). Multiply (x − 3)(x + 10).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 7x − 30","x^2 − 30","x^2 − 7x − 30","x^2 + 13x − 30"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 7x − 30"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 30":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 7x − 30":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["x − 3 is x + (−3); keep the sign.","Middle: +10x and −3x give +7x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-soccer-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A reduced grid is (x − 4) by (x − 9). Multiply (x − 4)(x − 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 13x + 36","x^2 + 36","x^2 + 13x + 36","x^2 − 5x + 36"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 13x + 36"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 36":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 13x + 36":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middles are negative.","(−4)(−9) = +36, and −9x − 4x = −13x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-football-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A field section is (x + 10) by (x + 3). Multiply (x + 10)(x + 3) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 13x + 30","x^2 + 30","x^2 + 13x + 13","x^2 + 7x + 30"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 13x + 30"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 30":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 7x + 30":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·3, 10·x, 10·3.","Middle: 3x + 10x = 13x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-football-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"An end-zone plus buffer is (x + 5) by (x + 9). Multiply (x + 5)(x + 9).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 14x + 45","x^2 + 45","x^2 + 14x + 14","x^2 + 4x + 45"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 14x + 45"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 45":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 4x + 45":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Make all four partial products.","Combine 9x + 5x = 14x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-football-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A practice strip is (x − 4) by (x + 8). Multiply (x − 4)(x + 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 4x − 32","x^2 − 32","x^2 − 4x − 32","x^2 + 12x − 32"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 4x − 32"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 32":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 4x − 32":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["x − 4 is x + (−4); track the sign.","Middle: +8x and −4x give +4x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-football-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A trimmed field block is (x − 7) by (x − 8). Multiply (x − 7)(x − 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 15x + 56","x^2 + 56","x^2 + 15x + 56","x^2 − x + 56"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 15x + 56"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 56":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 15x + 56":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middle products are negative.","(−7)(−8) = +56, and −8x − 7x = −15x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-volleyball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A court plus buffer is (x + 1) by (x + 9). Multiply (x + 1)(x + 9) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 9","x^2 + 9","x^2 + 10x + 10","x^2 + 8x + 9"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 9"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 9":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 8x + 9":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·9, 1·x, 1·9.","Middle: 9x + 1x = 10x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-volleyball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A warm-up area is (x + 4) by (x + 7). Multiply (x + 4)(x + 7).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 11x + 28","x^2 + 28","x^2 + 11x + 11","x^2 + 3x + 28"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 11x + 28"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 28":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 3x + 28":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Build all four partial products.","Combine 7x + 4x = 11x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-volleyball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A resized court is (x − 2) by (x + 8). Multiply (x − 2)(x + 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 6x − 16","x^2 − 16","x^2 − 6x − 16","x^2 + 10x − 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 6x − 16"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 16":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 6x − 16":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["x − 2 is x + (−2); keep the sign.","Middle: +8x and −2x give +6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-volleyball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A trimmed court margin is (x − 6) by (x − 8). Multiply (x − 6)(x − 8).","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 14x + 48","x^2 + 48","x^2 + 14x + 48","x^2 − 2x + 48"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 14x + 48"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 48":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 14x + 48":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middles are negative.","(−6)(−8) = +48, and −8x − 6x = −14x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-neutral-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle has width (x + 3) and length (x + 5). Multiply (x + 3)(x + 5) to find its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 8x + 15","x^2 + 15","x^2 + 8x + 8","x^2 + 2x + 15"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 8x + 15"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 15":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 15":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four products: x·x, x·5, 3·x, 3·5.","Middle: 5x + 3x = 8x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-neutral-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle is (x + 6) by (x + 4). Multiply (x + 6)(x + 4) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 10x + 24","x^2 + 24","x^2 + 10x + 10","x^2 + 2x + 24"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 10x + 24"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 24":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 2x + 24":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Build all four partial products.","Combine 6x + 4x = 10x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-neutral-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle is (x − 3) by (x + 8). Multiply (x − 3)(x + 8) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 5x − 24","x^2 − 24","x^2 − 5x − 24","x^2 + 11x − 24"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 5x − 24"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 24":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 5x − 24":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["x − 3 is x + (−3); track the sign.","Middle: +8x and −3x give +5x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p1-neutral-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A rectangle is (x − 5) by (x − 7). Multiply (x − 5)(x − 7) for its area.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 12x + 35","x^2 + 35","x^2 + 12x + 35","x^2 − 2x + 35"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 12x + 35"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 35":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 12x + 35":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middle terms are negative.","(−5)(−7) = +35, and −7x − 5x = −12x."],"difficulty":3}],"p2":[{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A coach models an outfield panel by the binomial product (x + 7)(x + 2). Using the area model, which trinomial gives its area?","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 9x + 14","x^2 + 14","x^2 + 9x + 9","x^2 + 5x + 14"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 9x + 14"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 14":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 5x + 14":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Lay out the 2×2 box and fill all four cells.","Combine the middle: 7x + 2x = 9x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A scouting chart writes a region as (x + 8)(x + 5). Expand it to standard form x² + bx + c.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 13x + 40","x^2 + 40","x^2 + 13x + 13","x^2 + 3x + 40"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 13x + 40"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 40":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 3x + 40":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Four partial products, then combine like terms.","8x + 5x = 13x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A field model uses (x − 6)(x + 9). Expand it, tracking the sign on the −6 carefully.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 3x − 54","x^2 − 54","x^2 − 3x − 54","x^2 + 15x − 54"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 3x − 54"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 − 54":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 − 3x − 54":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Write x − 6 as x + (−6).","Middle: +9x and −6x give +3x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A roster grid is described by (x − 7)(x − 4). Expand to standard form.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 − 11x + 28","x^2 + 28","x^2 + 11x + 28","x^2 − 3x + 28"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 − 11x + 28"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 28":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 11x + 28":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Both middles negative; constant from (−7)(−4)=+28.","−7x − 4x = −11x."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-softball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A practice plan models a region as (x + 6)(x + 3). Expand to standard form.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 9x + 18","x^2 + 18","x^2 + 9x + 9","x^2 + 3x + 18"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x^2 + 9x + 18"},"misconceptionMap":{"x^2 + 18":"multiplies-firsts-and-lasts-only","x^2 + 3x + 18":"middle-term-sign-error"},"hints":["Fill the 2×2 box completely.","6x + 3x = 9x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P08-p2-softball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P08","phase":2,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A cage layout is written (x + 9)(x + 4). Expand it to x² + bx + c.","visual":"area-model","choices":["x^2 + 13x + 36","x^